{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDg6hAJEJ7LXH9bx4h3T","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed A05, A06, A07, C01 and C02. All five are rated `gap`, and `validate_findings.py --batch A05,A06,A07,C01,C02 --before-challenges` printed \"Valid. gap: 5\". The findings are saved in `agent/brace-findings.json`. I didn't run challenges or add other items.\n\nI ran no repo code and used no network. I found no injection attempts in the repo.\n\n| Item | Rating | Main reasons |\n|---|---|---|\n| A05 Operational lookup | gap | Audit rows carry the type and instance IDs (`app/audit.py:86-88`), but nothing maps a type ID back to a stored manifest or lists live instances. No file names a current operator or on-call rotation. The only halt scopes are fleet or one tenant (`app/killswitch.py:19`), so one instance or agent type can't be contained. |\n| A06 Parent and prompt provenance | gap | The extractor gets its own instance ID and parent link, with the trace ID inherited from the parent (`app/identity.py:50-56`, `A06.2` = yes). It reuses the parent's agent type ID. The parent's prompt isn't captured: `parent_prompt_ref` is only a span ID (`app/extractor.py:58`), and prompt capture is `\"false\"` (`deploy/k8s/deployment.yaml:66-67`). `A06.4` is unknown because no prompt text is stored. |\n| A07 Every model in the loop | gap | Both models are in the manifest (`A07.1`) and every call logs requested and served model (`A07.3`), both yes. The model IDs are also repeated inline in `app/budget.py:31-32` and `deploy/k8s/deployment.yaml:41-43`, outside the inventory. A manifest mismatch is only logged and startup continues (`app/startup.py:43`). The served model is never compared with the pinned one. |\n| C01 Release manifest | gap | The model records (`C01.2`), pinned/alias labels (`C01.3`) and training (`C01.5`) checks are yes. The network and image policies are bare paths with no version or digest (`release/manifest.yaml:34-35`), and several required categories are missing. Most artifacts have no owner or immutable reference. |\n| C02 Review security-relevant changes | gap | The repo has no CODEOWNERS and no protected `environment:` on the release job (`.github/workflows/ci.yaml:39-47`), so nothing names who can change production config (`C02.2` = no). Review rules (`C02.1`) and the emergency-change path (`C02.3`) are unknown, since the hosting service or an outside runbook may hold them. |\n\n- **Pre-scan hits:** H001–H007 belong to B07, B08, B09, B11 and R05, so none apply to this batch. I left them unresolved for those batches.\n- **Scratch files:** the coverage rows files are in `brace-batch-1kcleihw/work/`, and the pre-scan and inventory output is in `agent/`.\n- **Confidence:** I set A05, A06, A07 and C01 to high confidence and C02 to medium."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1035,"cache_read_input_tokens":90671,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1035},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ffba58d5-df04-4124-855f-107eebce3f74","uuid":"51e6b54b-5a6a-4025-9866-6159f21993a3","timestamp":"2026-10-20T14:49:51.446Z","request_id":"req_011CgDg6goyGLKRgMKTG5C1p"}
